   600	## 7. CRITICAL FORK — what stands between `(9,6,2)` and a Keller map
   601	
   602	`(9,6,2)` is realized as a curve (AUD §6, re-verified in §1) and survives the
   603	representation gate (§5). It is therefore the campaign's strongest
   604	counterexample-candidate substrate to date, and the honest question is what is
   605	still missing. Four things are, in increasing order of cost.
   606	
   607	**(R1) The full braid-monodromy factorisation, not the product.** `rho_inf`-fixedness
   608	is one relation — the *product* of the local relations. A representation exists iff
   609	the nine-tuple `T` is fixed by **every** local braid. For this curve the
   610	factorisation census is exact (§1): eight simple vertical tangencies, in eight
   611	distinct fibres, at smooth points, each contributing a `sigma_i` whose fixed-tuple
   612	condition is the identification `(T)`: `xi_i = xi_{i+1}`; and **one** fibre,
   613	`x = 0`, carrying all four nodes, contributing four commuting `sigma_i^2` whose
   614	fixed-tuple condition is `(N_1)`: `[xi_i, xi_{i+1}] = 1`, satisfied exactly by
   615	disjoint transpositions. Exponent ledger `8*1 + 4*2 = 16 = 2 delta_aff + d - 1`:
   616	the census is complete, no local braid is missing.
   617	
   618	Two structural consequences are available without computing the transports:
   619	
   620	* the eight tangencies form a **tree** on the nine sheets. `p : C -> C` is degree
   621	  `9` with eight simple critical points and connected total space, so
   622	  Riemann–Hurwitz gives `1 = 9 - 8` and the eight sheet-transpositions generate a
   623	  transitive subgroup of `S_9` with eight edges on nine vertices: a spanning
   624	  tree. In `H_1` this collapses all nine meridians and gives `H_1 = Z`, as it must;
   625	  it does **not** force equality of the `phi`-images, because each ZvK relation is
   626	  `xi_a = w xi_b w^{-1}` for a transport word `w`. No cheap kill here, and none is
   627	  claimed.
   628	* the `x = 0` fibre pins `Pi` further than `sgn` does. `Pi = phi(gamma_inf)` is the
   629	  product of the nine fibre meridians; grouping them by the degeneration at
   630	  `x = 0` gives `Pi in V_4 * tau`, `tau := phi(g_9)` the meridian at the smooth
   631	  point `t = 0` (each node contributes a product of two disjoint transpositions,
   632	  which lies in the normal subgroup `V_4`). By §5, `Pi` is a **transposition** on
   633	  every surviving `(9,6,2)` class. Hence `Pi tau in V_4` forces `tau = Pi` or
   634	  `tau` disjoint from `Pi`: **two of the six transpositions**, not six. That is a
   635	  genuine additional pin on any realization, obtained from the curve.
   636	
   637	What is not available at desk scale is the transport data itself. Computing the
   638	eight tangency transports for this degree-9 curve and intersecting the nine fixed
   639	sets is a finite, decidable computation, and it is the **cheapest decisive next
   640	step**: it either produces an explicit `phi` on `pi_1(C^2 - D)` — the first in the
   641	campaign — or kills `(9,6,2)` outright. Typed `OPEN[REP-96-BM-FACTORISATION]`.
   642	
   643	**(R2) Covering-space realization (Riemann existence), and the source.** A `phi`
   644	fixed by the whole factorisation gives only a degree-4 branched cover `Y -> C^2`
   645	with branch locus `D` and meridian data `T`. A Keller map additionally requires
   646	the **source** to be the affine plane, `Y ~ C^2`, plus the normality and
   647	miracle-flatness step RK §1 records as gate-inserted into the `(6,4)` descent.
   648	Riemann existence supplies `Y` as a normal surface and nothing about its
   649	isomorphism type; `Y ~ C^2` follows from no promoted result and is not implied by
   650	`pi_1`. Then `F : Y = C^2 -> C^2` must have `Jac F in C^*` with non-properness set
   651	`A_F`. **This is the largest single gap, and it is not numerical.** Typed
   652	`OPEN[REP-96-SOURCE-IS-C2]`.
   653	
   654	**(R3) The `b = 0` / budget constraints.** Two distinct symbols `b` are in play and
   655	must not be merged: in THEOREM 7.B (all-degree H2 integration §1) `b = 0` is the
   656	count of dicriticals with affine image and `mu = 1`, a **consequence of H2**;
   657	in the reducible cage (`reducible-all-n-opus5-20260901.md:130-134`) `b` is the
   658	number of **branched components** of `A_F`, and `(RC2)` forces `b = 1` at
   659	`N = 4, 5`. I use only the second.
   660	
   661	The `N = 4` residual profile is a single row: core `(2,1,0)`, `W = (1,2)`
   662	(`ibid.:459`), i.e. `A_F` has one branched component `D_1` of weight `2` and one
   663	trivial-dicritical component of weight `1`; and `corr = 0` on both dicriticals, so
   664	the branched component carries **only double points of smooth branches**
   665	(`b0-reducible-n5-opus5-20260831.md:496-500`). Checked against the realized curve:
   666	its four affine singularities are ordinary nodes of two smooth branches
   667	(§1) — **consistent**. The generic-meridian datum matches too: `a^{(1)} = N - W_1 = 2`
   668	and independently `a^{(1)} = #Fix(transposition) = 2`. The budget therefore does
   669	not obstruct `(9,6,2)`; but it does demand a **second component**, of degree at
   670	least `2` (Lemma NL), about which the numerical type says nothing. A counterexample
   671	needs that companion curve as well.
   672	
   673	**(R4) The `(M')` identity.** `(M')`
   674	(`round1033-sheet-gate-opus5-20260831.md:442`) is
   675	`a(nu + s - 1) - sum_{p in Sing A_F} a_p = d nu - 1` with `1 <= a <= d-2`,
   676	`0 <= a_p <= a`, `nu = sum_p (r_p - 1)`, `s = #Sing A_F`, `d = N`. **Its
   677	hypotheses are Keller + (H2) + (H3)**, and `(H2)` is `A_F` irreducible. Two
   678	statements, kept apart:
   679	
   680	*Under `(H2)` it is fatal — and it is exactly the promoted `N = 4` H2 closure.*
   681	For a nodal `A_F` with `s` nodes, `nu = s`, so `(M'-def)` reads
   682	`sum_p (a - a_p) = (a-1) + s(4-a)`, whose left side is at most `s a`. At `a = 2`:
   683	`2s >= 1 + 2s`, false for every `s >= 0`. At `a = 1`: `s >= 3s`, false for every
   684	`s >= 1`. So no nodal `N = 4` residual survives `(M')` under `(H2)` — which
   685	reproduces the promoted "B0 holds at `N = 4` under H2". This is a control on my
   686	use of the identity, not a new kill.
   687	
   688	*The `(9,6,2)` candidate does not live under `(H2)`.* The `N = 4` residual is the
   689	reducible-`A_F` case (the H2 branch is closed), so only the block-free form
   690	applies:
   691	`sum_i a^{(i)} chi_c(D_i \ Sing D) + sum_p a_p = 1 - d chi_c(V)`
   692	(`ibid.:462-466`). Instantiating it on the `N = 4` profile — `D = D_1 u D_2`,
   693	`a^{(1)} = 2`, `a^{(2)} = N - W_2 = 3`, `D_1` with `s_1` nodes and normalization
   694	`A^1`, `D_2` with `sigma_2` nodes and `chi_c(D_2) = chi_2`, meeting `D_1`
   695	transversally in `j` points; `a_p = 0` at a node of `D_1` (two disjoint size-2
   696	clusters exhaust the four letters), `a_p = 1` at a transverse `D_1 u D_2` point
   697	(clusters `2 + 1`), `a_p = 2` at a node of `D_2` (clusters `1 + 1`) — the identity
   698	collapses to
   699	
   700	```text
   701	(7.1)     chi_2 + sigma_2 = 1 ,   i.e.   D_2 also has normalization A^1 ,
   702	```
   703	
   704	**with `s_1` cancelling identically.** So at the `N = 4` reducible profile `(M')`
   705	is *blind to the affine node count of the branched component*: it constrains only
   706	the companion component's topology. It neither kills nor supports `(9,6,2)`, and
   707	it must not be quoted as doing either. Typed `OPEN[REP-96-MPRIME-COMPANION]`: the
   708	identity becomes binding only once `D_2` is pinned.
   709	
   710	**Summary of the fork.** Between "`(9,6,2)` is a realized numerical type with a
   711	surviving `S_4` representation datum" and "a Keller counterexample exists" stand:
   712	`OPEN[REP-96-BM-FACTORISATION]` (finite, decidable, cheapest);
   713	`OPEN[REP-96-SOURCE-IS-C2]` (the hard geometric step);
   714	`OPEN[REP-96-MPRIME-COMPANION]` (needs `D_2`); plus the construction of `D_2`
   715	itself. **No promoted theorem kills `(9,6,2)`.** The row is alive on the merits,
   716	not by a gap in the search.
