The frozen log records the six fixed assignments only as a count; it serializes no non-generating tuples. I’m therefore replaying the exact frozen action locally, changing only the order in which the nine predicates are tested (an intersection is order-independent), so the six tuples and their generated subgroups can be stated explicitly. An early audit also found a metadata-only convention issue in the Sage-emitted `free_auto_F9`; I’m checking it against the actual enumerator path before deciding whether it affects the kill.
